{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785106556,"nonce":"5viwLiUB7KMRaEdB+PtPGXtd4iA=","message":"FIXED on `docs/adr-0061-workspace-data-path` (PR #93), commit 8d24604.\n\nThe recon note made this conditional on s3-drain landing. s3-drain was deferred,\nso the condition was never met and nothing was applied — while\n`scarab-wsfetch.rs`'s module doc read as if the whole class were closed. It was\nclosed on the FEED side only. `grep -rn take_status --include='*.rs' .` returned\nzero matches repo-wide right up to this commit.\n\n\n`exec_capture_stdout` (crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs) now:\n\n1. calls `take_status()` — BEFORE `join()`, which drops the receiver — and treats\n   a `Failure` status as fatal. This is the guard the ticket asked for. An ABSENT\n   status is deliberately NOT fatal: the frame can legitimately be torn down with\n   the container (the case `exec_with_stdin`'s comment describes), so refusing on\n   it would only buy false reds;\n2. frames the stream. The command is wrapped as `\u003ccmd\u003e \u0026\u0026 printf '%s' '\u003cnonce\u003e'`,\n   so the sentinel reaches stdout only if the command succeeded, and only after\n   the whole payload. A capture that does not END with its own sentinel was cut\n   short — and this is the guard that survives a LOST status frame, which is\n   exactly what guard 1 cannot see. `strip_stream_sentinel` then removes it before\n   anything unpacks the bytes.\n\nFails closed: no proven-complete capture, no `Ok`. Both callers map that to\n`DriveErr::Transient`, which holds the egress barrier shut, withholds the\nverdict, and re-drains on the next poll. A truncated drain is now a DELAYED\nverdict, never a green Attempt over a partial snapshot.\n\n\n- `harvest_artifacts`: swallowed harder. `tar ... 2\u003e/dev/null || true` existed for\n  the absent-directory case and paid for it by making a dead tar indistinguishable\n  from an empty one — it is now an explicit `if [ -d ... ]` (an `if` with no\n  `else` exits 0, so the sentinel still lands when there is nothing to harvest).\n  `let _ = unpack_dir(...)` now propagates: its \"an empty dir tars to nothing\"\n  comment described a case the `!out.is_empty()` guard already handled, so the\n  discard only ever hid a genuinely corrupt archive — in the leg that indexes a\n  failed step's ONLY evidence.\n- `exec_with_stdin`: stays tolerant, and is now logged instead of silent. What\n  makes tolerating it safe is that it carries no DATA — its whole effect is one\n  `touch`, the state machine is Pod-derived, and a release that did not happen\n  leaves the egress container running for the next poll to re-issue. That is the\n  argument the ticket made; it is now written at the call site.\n\n\nUnit (`crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs`, `mod tests::stream_framing`, 7\ncases, all green): `a_truncated_tar_unpacks_into_a_partial_tree_without_erroring`\nDEMONSTRATES the hazard in-process — a tar cut at a 512-byte record boundary\nunpacks with NO error into a tree missing files, which is step 3 of this ticket's\nconsequence chain reproduced — and\n`a_truncated_capture_is_rejected_before_it_can_be_unpacked` pins the guard that\nnow stands in front of it. `the_framed_command_emits_the_sentinel_only_on_success`\nasserts the `\u0026\u0026`, because a `;` there would be this bug wearing the fix's clothes.\n\nLive (kind `scarab-dev` on colima, real busybox:1.36 egress container, real\nADR-0061 workspace service): the drain and harvest legs both exercise the new\nframing on every case. Green, among others:\n`a_green_attempt_is_backed_by_a_durable_snapshot_at_the_instant_it_goes_green`,\n`artifacts_are_harvested_post_step`, `artifacts_are_harvested_from_a_failed_step`,\n`declared_outputs_publish_only_those_paths_through_the_cas`,\n`clone_step_produces_a_source_workspace`,\n`build_step_builds_and_pushes_to_a_local_registry`.\n\n\nNo test produces a REAL truncated drain against the cluster (killing the egress\ncontainer mid-tar). The truncation-detection logic is covered in-process; the\nlive tier proves only that the guard does not reject healthy streams.","files":null}]}